  "observed": [
    "The original creation/private-send/fresh-client recovery/history deduplication/revocation/joined close case remains passing in both algorithms.",
    "Public snapshot supplies actual Participant identity kind; wrong kind refuses admission. Add/update/remove/re-admit preserve stable Participant ID and advance membership epoch.",
    "Same-ID original admission replay projects current observer role/revision without duplicate admission. The old admission receipt refuses after re-admission into a new epoch.",
    "Typed Session controls create solo and group Sessions, accept/reject/cancel invitations, end Sessions and preserve scoped original operation references across a fresh client.",
    "All four Session update variants execute: role change, additive media upgrade, codec preferences and participant leave. The public canonical snapshot confirms the selected Participant left. Codec reconciliation references remain separate from local completion.",
    "A media upgrade produces distinct state and topology counters. The wrongly cast state value is refused without ending the Session, while the actual topology revision succeeds.",
    "Existing accepted Session receives another invitation; its newly invited Participant accepts under current topology/authority. The common outlines now skip only terminal Session states.",
    "Snapshot parsing is centralized with page/byte limits and scope/duplicate checks; ordinary application calls use no Store, private route IDs or provider APIs. Store access in fixtures is limited to trusted setup/revocation."
  ],
  "corrections": [
    "Store-source audit corrected the earlier Session precondition assignment; current SDK uses topology throughout and Rustdoc rejects the wrong revision family.",
    "Membership replies are authorized current projections, so their revision may exceed original+1 and their role may have changed. The SDK validates original identity, command scope, receipt and epoch-bound authority without falsely requiring the old role.",
    "Initial fixture guessed the seeded identity kind and assumed topology-only writes left state_revision unchanged. Current fixtures read public metadata and use the migration-defined media-plus-topology write path for a real divergent-revision check. Failed candidates03/04 remain private failures, not passes."
  ],
